{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve been having really bad stomach pain and going to the bathroom every 15 minutes with liquid stools. It feels just like my usual Crohn’s flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you said this started a few days ago? Did you do anything different when it started?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, on the third I was in the bathroom constantly. I bumped my prednisone up from 10mg to 40mg like I’ve done before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. You also mentioned flank pain—can you describe that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:21:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Started on the left side, but now it’s on the right. I’ve had kidney stones before, so I was worried it might be one passing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ll check for that. Any fever or chills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:24:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really a fever, but I feel like I’m burning up after each bowel movement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:25:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. We’ll run some tests. You also mentioned tingling in your arm and leg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:26:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, left arm and inner leg—electric-like pain. But it’s better this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:27:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good to hear. That may be related to your B12 deficiency. We’ll give you your monthly shot tomorrow as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2180-04-08 19:29:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I don’t want to fall behind on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night show your white count went up a bit, which fits with inflammation from your Crohn’s."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not unusual during a flare. Your kidney function and liver tests are normal, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the back pain? Could it be a stone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an X-ray and ultrasound. No blockage or hydronephrosis. But the ultrasound did show a small 7mm area of mineralization in your right kidney—likely a non-obstructing stone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not passing now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s not moving or blocking anything. That means your pain is likely musculoskeletal or referred from your abdomen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. What’s next for the Crohn’s?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:25:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing IV steroids and fluids. Your stool output has already decreased since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve only gone three times this morning—still loose, but better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2180-04-09 08:27:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’ll start you on a liquid diet soon and switch to oral prednisone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2180-04-09 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just got your urine results back—there’s mild blood, but no infection. Supports that the stone isn’t active."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2180-04-09 14:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I just need to drink more water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2180-04-09 14:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Stay hydrated. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2180-04-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs today look better. White count is coming down, and your electrolytes are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2180-04-10 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2180-04-10 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on oral oxycodone now, and we’re reducing the IV pain meds. How’s the pain level?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2180-04-10 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but manageable. Cramping mostly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2180-04-10 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. We’re adding steroid enemas to target the rectal inflammation directly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2180-04-10 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve never used those before. How do they work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2180-04-10 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They deliver anti-inflammatory medicine right to the area that’s inflamed. You’ll use one three times a day for a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2180-04-10 09:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re being discharged today. Your symptoms have improved significantly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue prednisone at 20mg daily, loperamide for stool control, and oxycodone as needed. Also, lidocaine patches for back discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the enemas?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, use the steroid enema three times a day. We’ll also keep your B12 injections monthly. Follow up with your GI doctor soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if your pain worsens or you develop fever or new back pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:38:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your blood culture is still pending, but we don’t suspect infection. We’ll notify you if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:41:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks for letting me know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2180-04-11 07:42:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2180-04-08 18:57:00",
    "admission_end": "2180-04-11 14:46:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of Crohn’s disease status post subtotal colectomy and ileorectal anastomosis, steroid-dependent and refractory to multiple biologics, was admitted for abdominal pain and increased liquid stool output consistent with a disease flare. He had self-increased his prednisone dose and presented with right-sided flank pain, raising concern for nephrolithiasis. Imaging showed no obstruction but revealed a nonobstructing 7mm right renal stone. He was treated with IV steroids, bowel rest, IV fluids, and pain management. His symptoms improved, with decreased stool frequency and pain. He transitioned to oral prednisone, oxycodone, and hydrocortisone enemas. His paresthesias resolved, and he received his monthly B12 injection. He was discharged home with a plan to follow up with gastroenterology, continuing steroid taper, and monitoring for stone passage.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of small intestine with large intestine",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Calculus of kidney",
      "Backache, unspecified",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Acquired absence of intestine (large) (small)",
      "Disturbance of skin sensation",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Other chronic pain"
    ]
  }
}
